        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): suppress stdout/stderr stream errors in sandbox subprocesses",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where stdout/stderr pipe errors from Codex sandbox subprocesses (both process RPC and streaming HTTP helper) could surface as unhandled Node stream errors, crashing the exec-server WebSocket bridge.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen a Codex sandbox process exits or its pipes are broken, the Node stream layer emits `error` events on stdout/stderr Readable streams. Without a listener, these bubble into an unhandled rejection that terminates the exec-server bridge. The sibling `http.ts` streaming helper path (`sandbox-exec-server/http.ts`) had the same gap.\n\nThe fix mirrors the same pattern used in `src/agents/sessions/exec.ts:177-178` and other sibling spawn paths: attach a no-op error listener to suppress the events while letting the process `close` handler remain authoritative.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCodex sandbox exec-server no longer crashes when a subprocess pipe breaks in either the process RPC or streaming HTTP path. Output collection and close signalling continue to work normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Before / after (processes.ts)**:\n\n```diff\n const child = spawn(command, args, { env: execSpec.env, stdio: [\"pipe\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] });\n managed.child = child;\n+// Output pipes may fail independently while the process is running.\n+const ignoreOutputStreamError = () => {};\n+child.stdout.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n+child.stderr.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n```\n\n**Before / after (http.ts)**:\n\n```diff\n const child = spawn(command, args, { env: execSpec.env, stdio: [\"pipe\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] });\n+\n+const ignoreOutputStreamError = () => {};\n+child.stdout.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n+child.stderr.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n```\n\n**Runtime proof**: Both paths exercised through the full sandbox exec-server WebSocket/JSON-RPC bridge. A child process writing 200 lines each to stdout/stderr is terminated mid-output; the bridge survives and a second process starts normally. The streaming HTTP subprocess path also returns valid HTTP status without crashing.\n\n```text\n$ npx vitest run --project extension-codex sandbox-exec-server\n\n ✓ sandbox-exec-server.test.ts (15 tests)\n ✓ sandbox-exec-server.fs.test.ts   (13 tests)\n ✓ sandbox-exec-server.http.test.ts  (7 tests)\n ✓ sandbox-exec-server.json-rpc.test.ts (2 tests)\n ✓ sandbox-exec-server.pipe-survival.test.ts (2 tests)\n   ✓ process bridge survives stdout/stderr pipe errors when child\n     is terminated rapidly (33ms)\n   ✓ http streaming bridge survives stdout/stderr pipe errors when\n     socket closes mid-stream (1ms)\n\n Test Files  5 passed (5)\n      Tests  40 passed (40)\n   Duration  5.22s\n```\n\n- The same no-op error listener pattern already exists in `src/agents/sessions/exec.ts:177-178` for the general agent session exec path, confirming this is the repo-standard approach.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/codex-processes-stream-errors",
